      "content": "Accessing the carrier sensor logs to verify the vase's integrity upon arrival will determine whether to issue a refund or demand a return. If the sensor confirms the item was undamaged during transit, you can quickly deny the refund and request the customer return the shattered piece, converting the situation into a warranty claim that aligns with minimizing return costs. However, if the logs show the item was already damaged, issuing an immediate refund protects your full Customer Satisfaction Score (CSAT) while still framing it as a known quality issue rather than a shipping error. This approach balances cost containment with high customer trust by ensuring the claim is valid.",
