      "content": "I just pulled up those sensor logs you mentioned. Interestingly, the sensors show the package was handled perfectly and there were zero impact or vibration alerts during transit. It looks like the damage didn't happen in the truck. Given that, you still think a refund is the way to go to keep CSAT up, or should we be more strict since the data suggests the customer might be mistaken or exaggerating?",
